== Shackle Quest No. 0 (Dust)==

As you enter the Court of Pain, [[Grand Master Glox]], sits in mediation. Without even looking up, he addresses you. 'The time has come for discipline. Read the note in your inventory and then hand it to me to begin your training.'

Newbie iksar monks start out with a Guild Summons in their inventory, which reads:

 This Broodling has reached the Age of Rebirth.
 The Broodling is called forth to Cabilis to begin training in the art of fist and tail.
 Within the walls of the Court of Pain shall I wait.
 This summons shall be presented to me upon arrival.
 Discipline awaits.
 <br>
 Grand Master Glox
 The Swifttail Cast

Give the summons to Grand Master Glox.

: Grand Master Glox breaks his meditation and quickly grabs your forearms. You feel the raw power in his heavily callused hands. Out of nowhere, his tail sweeps forward and places a small shackle upon your wrist. He then points southward towards Master Bain and returns to his meditation.

You receive a {{:Shackle of Dust}}.

Note: If you lose this newbie item, you can complete [[The Penance]] quest to replace it (available for all Iksar classes from their guildmaster).

== Shackle Quest No. 1 (Clay)==

:NOTE: need Amiable faction to trigger.

''Shackle of '''Dust''' IS NOT a prerequisite for this quest, but it is for Stone''

[[File:npc_master_raska.png|frame|Master Raska]]
You say, 'Hail, Master Raska'

: Master Raska says 'Hmmph!! Expect to be a great master such as I? Maybe. You still appear to be a [whiff].'

You say, 'What is a whiff?'

: Master Raska says 'A whiff is the sound of a tail striking air. A whiff is you. Inexperienced. I can help you. If you [want to earn the second shackle].'

You say, 'I want to earn the second shackle.' (need Amiable faction or higher; can't be sneak-quested)

: Master Raska says 'Then you shall perform the first rite. Take this pack. To the Outlands you will go. You will fill and combine the pack with one of each of the following - [[Goblin Scout Beads]], a [[Large Scorpion Pincer]], [[a froglok skipper]]'s [[skipping stone]] and a [[Sabertooth Cub Canine]]. Return the full first rite pack and you shall prove yourself a monk.'

You obtain a [[First Rite Pack]]. Fill it with:
{{CheckboxList}}
* 1 [[Goblin Scout Beads]] ([[Lake of Ill Omen]], Warsliks Woods or Lavastorm)
* 1 [[Large Scorpion Pincer]] ([[Field of Bone]])
* 1 [[Skipping Stone]] ([[Swamp of No Hope]]) Merchants on the second floor of the ruins might have these from players selling them.
* 1 [[Sabertooth Cub Canine]] (Lake of Ill Omen)
{{end}}

Combine to craft a [[Full First Rite Pack]], which you should hand in:

: Master Raska says 'You have succeeded, young ______! You have proven yourself a skilled monk. You will now wear the shackle of clay. You will now be required to increase your intensity of training in hopes that you may soon be able to earn your [shackle of stone].' 

<div class="facblock">
* Your faction standing with SwiftTails got better.
* Your faction standing with LegionofCabilis got better.
</div>

{{exp}}

You receive 4 gold pieces.

You receive your {{:Shackle of Clay}}.

== Shackle Quest No. 2 (Stone) ==

Note: Adventurers who have lost their [[Shackle of Dust]] and are looking to avoid [[The Penance]] may [[Multiquest]] this quest by creating a new Iksar monk and using their shackle. 

===Checklist===

{{CheckboxList}}
* Obtain Shackle of Dust
* Obtain Shackle of Clay
* Obtain two [[Iksar Bandit Mask]]s
* Turn in shackles and masks to Master Raska (to receive [[Shackle of Stone]])
{{end}}

===Walkthrough===

This is the second Monk Shackle quest. [[Master Raska]] is located at approximately 390.29, 113.16 in the Cabilis Monk Guild (The Court of Pain). After completing the previous Shackle quest (Shackle of Clay), Raska mentions the Shackle of Stone...

You say, 'Tell me about the shackle of stone'

: Master Raska says 'Interested in the shackle of stone are we? They are made for monks who have earned their first two shackles and are ready to climb up to the next rung. A monk who feels he is ready to wear the shackle of stone must first [perform the task of cleansing].'

You say, 'I am ready to perform the task of cleansing'

: Master Raska says 'Go forth to the outer gates and seek out the [[Iksar bandit]]s. They have refused to bow to the will of the empire and shall pay dearly for their traitorous ways. They often wear bandit masks. If you return with two bandit masks and the shackles of dust and clay then I shall reward you with the shackle of stone.'

The iksar bandits that drop the masks Raska is looking for spawn within and around the central pit in The [[Field of Bone]] and also near Kaesora city entrance.

Upon turning in the Shackle of Clay, Shackle of Dust, and the two [[Iksar Bandit Mask]]s, you'll receive your {{:Shackle of Stone}} and gain positive faction hits with the Legion of Cabilis and The Swift Tails.

Master Raska says, 'You will get nothing until I hold two bandit masks and the shackles of dust and clay.'
Master Raska says, 'You will get nothing until I hold two bandit masks and the shackles of dust and clay.'
Master Raska says, 'You will get nothing until I hold two bandit masks and the shackles of dust and clay.'
Master Raska says, 'You have done supremely, ______. You have earned your shackle of stone. Mistress Niska will now help you on your way to earning the shackle of rock. May the elements guide you to the next rung.'

<div class="facblock">
* Your faction standing with SwiftTails got better.
* Your faction standing with LegionofCabilis got better.
</div>

{{exp}}

You receive 3 gold pieces.

You receive your {{:Shackle of Stone}}.

